Welcome to boXiv — an archive for biology olympiads. This is where major updates and changes will be posted.

## What is boXiv?

boXiv aims to be the most comprehensive archive of high-school biology olympiad problems. It collects official question papers, solutions, answer sheets, and grading schemes for the canonical olympiads — from the well-known IBO down to national gems like INBO and ABO — and shines a light on the many lesser-known national and regional competitions too.

It is a fork of [phoXiv](https://phoxiv.org), the physics-olympiad archive, adapted for biology.

## Why?

Biology olympiad materials are scattered across dozens of national websites, personal folders, and dead links. Finding a complete set of problems and solutions for a given competition and year is often frustrating. boXiv brings them together in one fast, searchable, mobile-friendly place.

## How do I contribute?

Want to add problems, fix an error, or contribute a whole new olympiad? Sign in and head to the [contribute](/contribute) page, or open an issue or PR on [GitHub](https://github.com/darshdudhia/boXiv).

Browsing is, and always will be, open to everyone — no account required.